WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.580
A reported $6.9 billion Huawei license is not Qualcomm's deal, killing the logic folding claim. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 15. Tech power up, put that estimate on a Qualcomm Huawei license, and citing Bloomberg, attached it to logic folding. The first write-up casts the design as two sheets of silicon stacked vertically, with a 55% density gain and a 41% efficiency gain.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.420
as a route around sanctions and fab limits.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:39.120
At 630 UTC on October 6th, Qualcomm described a multi-year patent cross-license spanning

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.760
a range of technology fields.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.640
The terms stake confidential.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:48.900
Qualcomm said reports casting it as a net pay or are incorrect, and that claims tying the

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.160
agreement to logic fold are not accurate.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:57.620
Separately, Qualcomm agreed to buy certain Huawei non-cellular US patents across several

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.540
technology areas. Yesterday, the memory question was still allocation in pricing.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:11.700
SK Heinex has now finished joint validation of HBM-5 with TSMC's COOS, ADH-OC news reports.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.680
That check ties the next high-band with memory generation to TSMC's advanced packaging

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:20.440
flow, not to a memory test standing alone.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:27.540
Semiconductor Engineering's October 6th library ad includes a transistor paper from HUST,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:34.720
PolyU, UC Santa Barbara, and the National University of Singapore on ballistic P-type devices in

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:42.300
oxygen-doped tungsten-dicellinide monolayers aimed at low contact resistance. UC Santa Cruz added a

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.080
design space study of backside clock meshes for two nanometer gate all-around transistors with

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:55.080
backside power delivery. Syracuse University, FAU, Airlong, and Nernberg, and TU Dresden added

00:01:55.080 --> 00:02:03.040
Rapid, Rho parallel arithmetic inside DRAM. UC Berkeley and Furiosa AI added a characterization of

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.680
high bandwidth flash for serving large language models. Data Center Knowledge says rack level

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:14.480
batteries, battery energy storage systems, and solid state transformers are reopening where the

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.340
uninterruptible power supply sits in the power train.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.500
Uptime Institute's annual outage analysis, 2026,

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:25.640
found power problems behind more than one in five IT service

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.560
outages over the past three years.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.100
Among those power incidents, UPS failures

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.300
led at 39%, transfer switches at 34%

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.800
and generators at 28%.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.460
The same research names lithium ion UPS batteries

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:45.460
as a clear factor in a gradual rise in major data center fires

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:49.220
and says the rise may partly follow the pace of new builds

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.060
rather than the chemistry alone.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.260
Hyper-scale operators had already adopted

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:57.760
open-compute project direct current layouts with distributed

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.640
or rack-level UPS, including battery backup units

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.560
beside or instead of one central UPS.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.900
800 volt direct current in so-called AI factories

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:14.100
batteries, plus side-car power cabinets, stretches that distributed layout toward extreme

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:21.440
rack density. Morgan Stanley sees a 32-gigawatt shortfall by 2028, where the AI build-out meets

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:28.120
the power grid, Igor's lab reports. That gap is grid scale, not the rating of one campus.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:36.800
Trendforce via Big Go says TSMC plans to lift mature process prices by about 3-10% starting

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:43.760
in January next year. An extra 6-8% on 2 nanometer wafer prices is reported for the first quarter

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:50.240
of next year, tied to manufacturing costs and electricity. Some individual customers have already

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:57.820
had 10-20% reflected in their prices. Makers of power management ICs, display driver ICs and

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:03.640
microcontrollers are weighing product increases of 5% to double-digit levels from late this year

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:09.760
into early next year. SMIC has already raised prices on some tight capacity for

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:14.240
waifers starting in the third quarter. Second quarter average wafer selling price

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:21.940
rose 5.7% from the prior quarter. An utilization hit 93.7%. Some buyers are

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.760
advancing orders, pointing to capacity risk from middle-east conflict

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:31.940
concerns, and rising AI demand. Digitimes reports that TSMC's expansion has

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:38.620
taken Dai Yi Chang Technologies orders past 10 billion new Taiwan dollars. Visibility on those

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:44.980
orders runs through 2028. Take it apart at the standard cell, and a track is simply a wiring

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:51.660
lane that sets how tall that cell is. On IMEX Roadmap, as semiconductor engineering published it,

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:58.840
gate all around nanosheets carry logic through the A10 generation, and there allow 5.5 track cells.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:06.640
From A7, IMEX says the industry may stack P type on N type in a complimentary FET, so

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:12.720
the two polarities no longer sit side by side, and the cell can fall to 4.5 tracks and below.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.820
Drive that stack harder and the same roadmap puts the cell at 3 tracks, which IMEX says

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.480
can extend classical CMOS at least to the A3 node.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:29.200
The shorter cell still needs contacts, gates, and power on the buried device, so iMac treats a

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:35.220
backside contact and a gate stack that can set more than one threshold as complementary FET

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:41.140
modules. The newer design study adds a sequential cell that can be split gate or common gate.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:47.760
Split gate leaves the two devices independently controllable, which logic and SRAM both need.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.620
Common Gate is the tighter choice when the pair should switch as one.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:58.720
That SRAM study lands on a 5-track plus 1 complementary FET bit cell, and a companion

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:03.780
study works back and route ability, because a short cell fails if the wires above it

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.460
cannot escape.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.500
At A7, IMEC also leaves CMOS 2.0 on the table.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:15.220
Split a system on chip into heterogeneous tiers and stitch them with 3D interconnects,

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.000
or keep pushing nano sheets with power from the front or the back.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:23.000
The stacked cell stops earning its place once an independent gate

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.220
and a backside contact cannot reach the buried device,

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.680
without handing the saved track height back to extra routing.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.060
On the horizon, TSMC's mature process price increases

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.380
are planned to start in January next year,

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.960
in trend forces account via big go.

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:43.280
An additional 6-8% on 2 nanometer wafer prices

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.000
is set for the first quarter of next year on that same reporting.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:53.620
Before we go, the nearest dated step is that January mature process price rise at TSMC.

